# shellcheck configuration for the scripts under scripts/.
#
# SC2016 ("expressions don't expand in single quotes") fires on every
# embedded jq, awk, and sed program that uses the embedded language's own
# $variable, because it cannot tell the embedded program from a shell
# string. In single quotes the shell correctly does not expand, and the
# embedded language expands its own variables. The scripts embed enough
# jq that a per-site suppression in each of them would cost more than
# the check is worth, and the check is not load-bearing here: no shell
# code in this repo wants a $variable expanded inside single quotes.
#
# The one site that does want deliberate word splitting, an ssh option
# string, carries an inline suppression where the intent is visible.
disable=SC2016
